    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0625",
      "reading_order": 951,
      "section": "Detailed description",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 62.23,
        "t": 493.26099999999997,
        "r": 528.7487999999995,
        "b": 454.684
      },
      "content": "The oil cooler bypass valve (BV1) starts closing the bypass line and opening the oil supply line from the main oil cooler (Co) at the lower limit of its temperature range. At the upper limit of its temperature range, the bypass line is completely closed and all the oil flows through the main oil cooler.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_932",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_5",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_5",
          "title": "5       Energy recovery (optional)"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_932",
          "title": "Detailed description"
        }
      ],
      "page": 90,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0626",
      "reading_order": 952,
      "section": "Detailed description",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 62.23,
        "t": 447.721,
        "r": 537.0108999999993,
        "b": 395.9440000000001
      },
      "content": "BV1 must have a higher opening temperature (set point) than BV2 in order to prevent the heat from being dissipated in the compressor oil cooler (Co) before the warm oil is fed to the oil/water heat exchanger when using the compression heat as source for energy recovery. Thermostat BV1 starts to open at 75 °C and is completely open at 90 °C.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_932",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_5",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_5",
          "title": "5       Energy recovery (optional)"
        },
